IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`

-- Canada Disability Benefit Regulations (SOR/2025-35), sections 17 to 19, 30 and 31 --
-- CHANGING A DECISION, ASKING THE MINISTER TO RECONSIDER IT, AND EXTENDING THE TIME.
--
-- The Minister's judgments ("satisfied", "reasonable time") are plain BOOLEAN inputs. The
-- text does not say how long an extension is (s 19(3) says the Minister "must allow an
-- extension of time" and no more), so how far the Minister extended is an input too.

§ `Regulations s 17 -- Amendment or rescission`

-- 17: the Minister may amend or rescind a decision the Minister made, on the basis of new facts.
-- src:192 | 17 The Minister may, on the basis of new facts, amend or rescind any decision made by the Minister.
@ref Regulations s 17 (src:192)
GIVEN `the Minister made the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `new facts have come to the Minister's attention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may amend or rescind the decision` `the Minister made the decision` `new facts have come to the Minister's attention` MEANS
        `the Minister made the decision`
    AND `new facts have come to the Minister's attention`

§ `Regulations s 18 -- Reconsideration of benefit`

-- 18(1) and 18(2): a person who is dissatisfied with a decision that no benefit be paid, a
-- decision about the amount of a benefit, or a penalty decision under s 35 (or its amount),
-- may ask the Minister to reconsider it. Other kinds of decision are not covered by s 18(1)
-- or (2).
-- src:194 | 18 (1) Subject to section 19, a person who is dissatisfied with a decision made under the Act or these Regulations that no benefit be paid to them, or respecting the amount of a benefit that the person has received or will receive, may, within 180 days after the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision, make a request to the Minister for a reconsideration of that decision.
-- src:195 | Reconsideration of penalty
-- src:196 | (2) Subject to section 19, a person against whom a penalty has been imposed by the Minister under section 35 and who is dissatisfied with that decision or with the amount of the penalty may, within 180 days after the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision, make a request to the Minister for a reconsideration of that decision.
@ref Regulations s 18(1) and (2) (src:194-196)
GIVEN request IS A `Request for reconsideration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the decision is one the person may ask the Minister to reconsider` request MEANS
        request's `the person is dissatisfied with the decision`
    AND (CONSIDER request's `the decision`
         WHEN `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a decision respecting the amount of a benefit that the person has received or will receive` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a decision imposing a penalty under section 35` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a decision on a request for reconsideration made under subsection 18(4)` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `a decision on a request for an extension of time made under subsection 19(4)` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `any other decision` THEN FALSE)

-- 18(1) and (2): within 180 days after the day the person is notified in writing. Day 1 is
-- the day after the notice.
@ref Regulations s 18(1) and (2) (src:194-196)
GIVEN `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the 180 days to ask the Minister to reconsider` `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` MEANS
    `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` PLUS 180

@ref Regulations s 18(1) and (2) (src:194-196); s 19(3) (src:209)
GIVEN request IS A `Request for reconsideration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the request was made in time` request MEANS
        request's `the day the request was made` AT MOST `the last day of the 180 days to ask the Minister to reconsider` (request's `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision`)
     OR (CONSIDER request's `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST extended THEN request's `the day the request was made` AT MOST extended)

-- 18(3): in writing to the Minister, with (a) the name and address of the applicant or
-- beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the application's reference number,
-- (b) if that person is incapable of managing their own affairs, the name and address of their
-- representative, and (c) the decision and a statement of the reasons and facts.
-- src:198 | (3) A request for reconsideration must be made in writing to the Minister and contain the following information:
-- src:199 | (a) the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary, as applicable, and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number assigned to the benefit application;
-- src:200 | (b) if the person referred to in paragraph (a) is incapable of managing their own affairs, the name and address of their representative; and
-- src:201 | (c) the decision for which a request for reconsideration is being made and a statement of the reasons and facts that form the basis of that request.
@ref Regulations s 18(3) (src:198-201)
GIVEN request IS A `Request for reconsideration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the request has the contents the Regulations require` request MEANS
        request's `the request is made in writing to the Minister`
    AND request's `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application`
    AND (   NOT request's `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs`
         OR request's `the request gives the name and address of their representative`)
    AND request's `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request`

-- 18(4): once a proper request is made in time, the Minister must reconsider within a
-- reasonable time and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reasons. The
-- Minister may confirm, amend or rescind the decision, approve payment, determine the amount
-- or determine that no benefit is payable; none of that depends on the person.
-- src:202 | Minister’s decision
-- src:203 | (4) The Minister must, within a reasonable time, reconsider the decision referred to in the request and may confirm, amend or rescind it, and may approve payment of a benefit, determine the amount of a benefit or determine that no benefit is payable. In all cases, the Minister must notify in writing the person who made the request of the Minister’s decision and the reasons for it.
@ref Regulations s 18(4) (src:202-203)
GIVEN request IS A `Request for reconsideration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister must reconsider the decision and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reasons` request MEANS
        `the decision is one the person may ask the Minister to reconsider` request
    AND `the request was made in time` request
    AND `the request has the contents the Regulations require` request

§ `Regulations s 19 -- Request for extension`

-- 19(1): the request for an extension must be made not later than 185 days after the end of
-- the 180 days.
-- src:205 | 19 (1) A person may request that the Minister extend the 180‑day period referred to in subsections 18(1) and (2) not later than 185 days after the end of that period.
@ref Regulations s 19(1) (src:205)
GIVEN `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to ask the Minister to extend the 180 days` `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` MEANS
    `the last day of the 180 days to ask the Minister to reconsider` `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` PLUS 185

@ref Regulations s 19(1) (src:205)
GIVEN `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the day the request for an extension was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the request for an extension was made in time` `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` `the day the request for an extension was made` MEANS
    `the day the request for an extension was made` AT MOST `the last day to ask the Minister to extend the 180 days` `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision`

-- 19(3): the Minister must allow an extension if satisfied that at least one of the six
-- situations has occurred and has significantly impacted the person's ability to meet the time.
-- The situation is named so that the person can say which one; the Minister's satisfaction is
-- the judgment.
-- src:209 | (3) The Minister must allow an extension of time if the Minister is satisfied that at least one of the following situations has occurred and has significantly impacted the ability of the person referred to in subsection (1) to respect the time period:
-- src:210 | (a) an emergency, if a state of emergency has been declared by a federal or provincial minister under federal or provincial law;
-- src:211 | (b) a natural or human‑made disaster, such as a flood or fire;
-- src:212 | (c) a civil disturbance, such as a riot;
-- src:213 | (d) a disruption in public services, such as a strike;
-- src:214 | (e) a serious accident, injury or illness suffered by the person; or
-- src:215 | (f) an emotional or mental distress suffered by the person, such as from a death in their family.
@ref Regulations s 19(3) (src:209-215)
GIVEN situation IS A `Situation affecting a time limit`
      `the Minister is satisfied that the situation has occurred and has significantly impacted the person's ability to respect the time period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister must allow an extension of time` situation `the Minister is satisfied that the situation has occurred and has significantly impacted the person's ability to respect the time period` MEANS
        `the Minister is satisfied that the situation has occurred and has significantly impacted the person's ability to respect the time period`
    AND (CONSIDER situation
         WHEN `an emergency, if a state of emergency has been declared by a federal or provincial minister under federal or provincial law` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a natural or human-made disaster, such as a flood or fire` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a civil disturbance, such as a riot` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a disruption in public services, such as a strike` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a serious accident, injury or illness suffered by the person` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an emotional or mental distress suffered by the person, such as from a death in their family` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE)

-- 19(2) and 19(4): a request for an extension must be made in the form and manner the
-- Minister specifies (the specification is not in the text, so whether it was is asked as
-- a fact); once one is made in time the Minister must consider it within a reasonable time
-- and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reason.
-- src:207 | (2) A request for an extension of time must be made in the form and manner specified by the Minister.
-- src:217 | (4) The Minister must consider a request for an extension of time within a reasonable time and must notify, in writing, the person who made the request of the Minister’s decision and the reason for it.
@ref Regulations s 19(2) (src:207); s 19(4) (src:217)
GIVEN `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the day the request for an extension was made` IS A DATE
      `the request for an extension was made in the form and manner specified by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister must consider the request for an extension and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reason` `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` `the day the request for an extension was made` `the request for an extension was made in the form and manner specified by the Minister` MEANS
        `the request for an extension was made in the form and manner specified by the Minister`
    AND `the request for an extension was made in time` `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` `the day the request for an extension was made`

§ `Regulations s 31 -- Denial of benefit due to administrative error`

-- 31: the Minister must take the remedial action the Minister considers appropriate if
-- satisfied that an administrative error led to a person being denied a benefit, or a portion
-- of it, to which they would have been entitled.
-- src:267 | 31 If the Minister is satisfied that, as a result of an administrative error in the administration of the Act or these Regulations, any person has been denied a benefit, or a portion of a benefit, to which that person would have been entitled, the Minister must take any remedial action that the Minister considers appropriate to place the person in the position that they would be in had the administrative error not been made.
@ref Regulations s 31 (src:267)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that there was an administrative error in the administration of the Act or these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was denied a benefit or a portion of a benefit as a result of the error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would have been entitled to what they were denied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister must take remedial action to put the person in the position they would be in` `the Minister is satisfied that there was an administrative error in the administration of the Act or these Regulations` `the person was denied a benefit or a portion of a benefit as a result of the error` `the person would have been entitled to what they were denied` MEANS
        `the Minister is satisfied that there was an administrative error in the administration of the Act or these Regulations`
    AND `the person was denied a benefit or a portion of a benefit as a result of the error`
    AND `the person would have been entitled to what they were denied`
